#4471 holds **412 reports** (427 rows in the export; 15 are repeats of an id). They are not one bug.
They were merged because they look alike: a date on the wrong day. Read by tenant and by body,
they are two problems.

<Callout>
Not one known issue. Two problems, and only one has a fix queued.
</Callout>

## The two problems

| problem | reports | what happens | who |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **parser** | 379 | The shared parser reads every date month first, so day-first tenants get flipped dates. This is what #4471 was opened for. | all 11 tenants |
| **hint** | 33 | `booking-v3` prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People at day-first tenants type what the hint says, and the form reads it their way. A different bug: fixing the parser does not fix it. | alder.physio, copper.studio, pale.harbour (form channel only) |

379 + 33 = 412.

5 of the 379 `parser` reports read as a one-day move, not a flip (R-41202, R-41209, R-41236, R-41344, R-41620). The desk files them under `parser` by tenant, and so does this page. They may be a time zone problem; that is not confirmed.

## What the table below counts

The table is computed from the export and shows the same 379 and 33. The 5 one-day moves are footnoted under it.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## Intake tags

Intake guessed the cause from the reporter's browser. It is wrong often: 15 of the 33 `hint` reports
were tagged `parser`, and 23 of the 379 `parser` reports were tagged `hint`. Do not triage on the tag.

## Lessons

- Reports that look alike are not one bug. Count by cause, not by subject line (see [triage](/kb/triage/dedupe)).
- Read the body. 5 reports describe a one-day shift, not a flip. Check them before you close the ticket.


